.policy "ruff-air002-airflow-dag-no-schedule-argument" revision 2
.description "Give every Airflow Dag an explicit schedule; the implicit default changed from daily to none in Airflow 3, silently stopping Dags that relied on it."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff AIR002 (Airflow): a `DAG(…)` or `@dag(…)` call without `schedule`, `schedule_interval` or `timetable`.
// The default schedule changed in Airflow 3 (from daily to none), so the Dag's behaviour depends on the
// version. The callee is any `airflow….DAG` or `airflow….dag`; only in a file that imports airflow. Reported
// at the call (for a decorator, its call after the `@`).
//   DAG(dag_id="class_default_schedule")       ← AIR002
//   @dag()                                     ← AIR002
//   DAG(dag_id="x", schedule="@hourly")        not reported
#include "python/misc-airflow.rr"

.violation AIR002(at: node) code "AIR002"
    "Pass an explicit `schedule=` to this Dag (`schedule=None` if it should only run when triggered); relying on the default changes behaviour between Airflow 2 and 3."
    suppress ruff "AIR002"
AIR002(c) :- air_call(c, q), air_dag(q), !call_kwarg(c, "schedule", _), !call_kwarg(c, "schedule_interval", _),
    !call_kwarg(c, "timetable", _).
